## 3. List Operations (opsForList)

Ordered list. Can add from left or right.

```java
public void listExamples() {

    ListOperations<String, Object> ops = 
                    redisTemplate.opsForList();

    // Push to RIGHT (end of list)
    ops.rightPush("notifications:user1", "Order placed");
    ops.rightPush("notifications:user1", "Order shipped");
    ops.rightPush("notifications:user1", "Order delivered");

    // Push to LEFT (start of list)
    ops.leftPush("notifications:user1", "New message");

    // Get all items (0 to -1 means all)
    List<Object> all = ops.range("notifications:user1", 0, -1);

    // Get first 5 items
    List<Object> first5 = ops.range("notifications:user1", 0, 4);

    // Pop from left (remove and return)
    String first = (String) ops.leftPop("notifications:user1");

    // Size of list
    Long size = ops.size("notifications:user1");

    // Keep only last 100 items (trim old notifications)
    ops.trim("notifications:user1", -100, -1);
}
```

Redis stores:
```
notifications:user1 → ["New message",
                        "Order placed",
                        "Order shipped",
                        "Order delivered"]
```

