## 4. Set Operations (opsForSet)

Unique values only. No duplicates.

```java
public void setExamples() {

    SetOperations<String, Object> ops = 
                    redisTemplate.opsForSet();

    // Add members
    ops.add("onlineUsers", "user1", "user2", "user3");
    ops.add("onlineUsers", "user1"); // duplicate - ignored!

    // Check if member exists
    Boolean isOnline = ops.isMember("onlineUsers", "user1");

    // Get all members
    Set<Object> allOnline = ops.members("onlineUsers");

    // Remove member
    ops.remove("onlineUsers", "user1");

    // Count members
    Long count = ops.size("onlineUsers");

    // Set operations
    Set<Object> common  = ops.intersect("onlineUsers", "premiumUsers");
    Set<Object> allUsers = ops.union("onlineUsers", "premiumUsers");
    Set<Object> diff    = ops.difference("onlineUsers", "premiumUsers");
}
```

