## 5. ZSet - Sorted Set (opsForZSet)

Like Set but each member has a **score** for ranking.

```java
public void zsetExamples() {

    ZSetOperations<String, Object> ops = 
                    redisTemplate.opsForZSet();

    // Add with score
    ops.add("leaderboard", "PlayerA", 9500);
    ops.add("leaderboard", "PlayerB", 8200);
    ops.add("leaderboard", "PlayerC", 9800);
    ops.add("leaderboard", "PlayerD", 7100);

    // Get top 3 (highest score first)
    Set<Object> top3 = ops.reverseRange("leaderboard", 0, 2);
    // Returns: [PlayerC, PlayerA, PlayerB]

    // Get rank of a player
    Long rank = ops.reverseRank("leaderboard", "PlayerA");
    // Returns: 1 (0 based, PlayerC is 0)

    // Get score
    Double score = ops.score("leaderboard", "PlayerA");
    // Returns: 9500.0

    // Increment score
    ops.incrementScore("leaderboard", "PlayerB", 500);
    // PlayerB score becomes 8700
}
```

Redis stores:
```
leaderboard
  PlayerD → 7100
  PlayerB → 8200
  PlayerA → 9500
  PlayerC → 9800  ← highest
```

