## RedisTemplate vs @Cacheable

```
Use @Cacheable when:
✅ Simple method result caching
✅ Don't want to write boilerplate
✅ TTL based expiry is enough

Use RedisTemplate when:
✅ Need Lists, Sets, ZSets
✅ Need to update single fields (Hash)
✅ Building leaderboards, sessions
✅ Need manual control over keys
✅ Pub/Sub messaging
✅ Distributed locking
```

---

## Summary of Operations

| Structure | Method | Use Case |
|---|---|---|
| String | `opsForValue()` | Simple cache, counters |
| Hash | `opsForHash()` | Object fields, sessions |
| List | `opsForList()` | Notifications, queues |
| Set | `opsForSet()` | Online users, tags |
| ZSet | `opsForZSet()` | Leaderboards, rankings |

